---
const states = [
  { state:'AUTHORITY_UNVERIFIED', why:'An explicit attestation operation lacks current evidence.', action:'Keep that proof claim unproved and inspect its applicable host-owned evidence boundary. Ordinary authorized work still follows actual permissions and checks; preserve receipts without relabelling or inventing them.' },
  { state:'DRAFT_BINDING', why:'The requested operation requires a different specification binding.', action:'Inspect the selected identity and the operation that failed. Use native plan-binding maintenance for ordinary authoring; an explicit attestation operation retains its separate evidence requirements. Advisory eligibility and draft status are not execution permission.' },
  { state:'IN_PROGRESS', why:'An interrupted task may have changed files without finishing its review.', action:'Inspect those files and the recorded task state. Reconcile through the owning workflow before redispatch.' },
  { state:'REVIEW', why:'Implementation was marked ready for review.', action:'Inspect actual checks and applicable review requirements. The label establishes neither a passing test nor an independent review.' },
  { state:'DONE', why:'Implementation completion was recorded.', action:'Read actual check outcomes and report missing, failed or unrun verification separately. Continue authorized work while preserving real dependencies and user stops.' },
  { state:'BLOCKED', why:'A hard boundary or exhausted recovery strategy stopped this task.', action:'Resolve its specific reason. Preserve the failed strategy and attempt record; continue only independent authorized work.' },
  { state:'STALE_CURSOR', why:'A contributing specification, plan or authority record changed after the read.', action:'Read the current context again and reconsider the action. Never force the old cursor.' },
  { state:'RECOVERY_REQUIRED', why:'A transaction needs inspection before its outcome is known.', action:'Use the recorded operation ID and the recovery path. Do not replay the write with a new ID or remove its journal.' },
];
---
<div class="ca-recovery ca-exhibit" data-example="recovery">
  <p class="ca-kicker">Read the reason before retrying</p>
  <p>These are explanations of task states and diagnostic codes, not live state from your repository.</p>
  {states.map((entry) => <details><summary><code>{entry.state}</code><span>{entry.why}</span></summary><p><strong>Next safe action:</strong> {entry.action}</p></details>)}
  <p class="ca-exhibit-footnote">Progress labels, advisory scheduling and explicit attestation are distinct. Expanding these explanations never changes a task or grants permission.</p>
</div>
